[0m[0m
For [38;5;10msize >= 0x3FFF_FFFD[0m, [38;5;10msize*4[0m wraps such that [38;5;10mcap[0m becomes a small [3mpositive[23m number ([38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m → [38;5;10mcap == 3[0m), so [38;5;10mcalloc[0m succeeds and the C loop then writes ~2.8 GiB past a 3-byte buffer. That is undefined behaviour with no observable ground truth, so it is excluded from the differential suite and documented in [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m row 7. I verified the adjacent bands instead: [38;5;10m[0x2000_0000, 0x3FFF_FFFC][0m returns [38;5;10mNULL[0m in both (cap negative), and [38;5;10m0x1FFF_FFFF[0m — one step below the threshold, where the loop really runs — passes with a genuine 512 MiB source buffer.[0m[0m
